# CHANGED ON THE THOR AFTER PHASES 0-5 (2026-10-06 17:25 and later; NOT part of the parity reference):
# ~/.local got `pip install --user ultralytics` (PyPI) and then
# `pip install --user --force-reinstall --no-deps torch torchvision --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu130`:
#   torch 2.14.1+cu130, torchvision 0.29.1+cu130, ultralytics 8.4.174, opencv-python 4.11.0.86, triton 3.8.0,
#   and PyPI CUDA 13: cuda-toolkit 13.0.3.0, nvidia-cudnn-cu13 9.24.0.43, nvidia-cublas 13.1.1.3,
#   nvidia-nccl-cu13, nvidia-cusparselt-cu13, nvidia-nvshmem-cu13, ... (pip_user.txt).
# setuptools in ~/.local: 84.0.0 at 14:27, replaced by 79.0.1 at 14:42 on 2026-10-07 (someone was working there).
# This is the PyPI-CUDA pattern the Phase 5d hard rule forbids for the image (and backlog M9's CUDA safety
# rule); it is reported, not touched. It also means "no torch on the Thor" (D0, M9) is no longer true.
torch                  NONE_IN_REFERENCE    # Orin image: 2.8.0 cp312 (jetson-ai-lab jp6/cu129); Orin Humble: 2.11.0 cp310 cu126
torchvision            NONE_IN_REFERENCE    # Orin image: 0.23.0 cp312; Orin Humble: 0.26.0
ultralytics            8.4.90               # = Orin Humble (the YOLO reference is the Orin's own Humble install); Thor ~/.local now 8.4.174
opencv_python          4.11.0.86            # = Orin Humble and Thor ~/.local
# The TensorRT engine export (export_yolo_engine.sh: Ultralytics -> ONNX -> TensorRT, simplify=True).
# NOT Thor values: the Orin Humble host's export toolchain (output/perf/yolo_recon.md); every dependency pinned
# in the Dockerfile's py stage (ml_dtypes 0.5.4, protobuf 7.36.2, coloredlogs 15.0.1, flatbuffers 25.12.19, ...).
onnx                   1.22.0               # = Orin Humble
onnxslim               0.1.94               # = Orin Humble
onnxruntime            1.23.2               # = Orin Humble (CPU build); also faster-whisper's, through the gateway venv

